  <Comments>Version 1.1, 26 Jan 24
Changes in Version 1.1:
-Added speed multiplier script for enemies.
Feel free to repost this table as it might not be maintained, please give credit for any used material.
Some scripts use booleans to enable/disable features. You can edit the defined byte (db) value within the script to change the default setting at the botton of the [ENABLE] section. E.g, this will change infinite health to off on script activation:
bInfHealth:
db 1 &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; db 0
Patching this table may become difficult in the future. To patch, add wildcards to AOB scans and extend their length if necessary, update any changed offsets. Instructions may need to be found again with the debugger. The most important one is the player instance of class. There are some pointers under WIP that I used to find the instruction that accesses player instance. Remove offsets from them, as they are pointers to a StatComponent where the stamina value is located. As of 26/01/24, stamina is found here:
(((PlayerInstance+848)+E0)+28)+3C
This translates to PlayerInstance&gt;StatComponent&gt;StatData&gt;StatList&gt;StaminaValue
Keep in mind when scanning for stamina, it does not reach 0. Try not to scan with empty stamina. You can then find what only accesses PlayerInstance+0 (I used the first instruction) to update the Player pointer scipt by reversing these offsets.
Hopefully at this point the player structure I have assigned to table will be accurate, and you can update most scripts.
Most likely the AOB scans will be the issue. Some scripts use offsets in PlayerInstance or instances of other objects, if they change they will need to be updated too.
</Comments>
</CheatTable>
